## P3-05 — Atomic candidate activation

**Files touched (exhaustive):**
- `crates/application/src/activation.rs` (new — only source file)
- `crates/application/src/lib.rs` (added `pub mod activation;`)
- `crates/application/Cargo.toml` — unchanged (no new deps; `async_trait`, `serde`, `thiserror`, `tokio` already present)

**What it implements (binding source: ARCHITECTURE.md §8.4 + A-04):**
- **`ActivationStore`** — phased storage-side port with strict A-04 ordering: `current_active_pointer` (read-only) → `stage_candidate_pointer` (writes pending pointer, live pointer untouched) → `verify_candidate_readable` (confirms staged candidate opens) → `commit_active_pointer` (the *only* method that mutates the live pointer, guarded by `expected_previous`, journal row written in the same transaction) → `abort_staged_candidate` / `quarantine_staged_candidate` (clean-up paths). Each outcome-persisting method writes the `install_transactions` row in the same critical section as its state change.
- **`ActivationStoreError`** — six variants discriminating transient (`StorageUnavailable`, `CandidateNotReadable`, `PointerContended`) from candidate-trust (`CandidateMissing`, `CandidateIntegrityFailed`, `QuarantineFailed`) failures, with `From` into the existing `ActivationError`.
- **`InstallTransactionRecord` + `ActivationTransactionOutcome`** — `install_transactions` row shape; serde `rename_all = "snake_case"` so the wire form of an outcome matches `library::ActivationOutcome`'s `kind` tag whether read live or from the journal.
- **`coordinate_activation`** — application-layer coordinator driving the four-phase protocol: observe → stage → verify → commit. On every non-commit path it cleans up (`abort_*` or `quarantine_*`) so the previously-active pack stays readable (A-04) and untrusted bytes are quarantined (A-07).

**Re-export contract:** re-exports `ActivationRequest`/`ActivationOutcome`/`ActivationError` from `crate::library` so callers name every activation item from one path without duplicating the §8.4 handoff surface.

**Tests (real in-memory `ActivationStore`, no mocks):** 11 tests covering happy-path commit+journal atomicity, fresh install (`None` previous), every A-04 failure path (observe/stage/verify-not-readable/verify-integrity/verify-missing/commit-contention/commit-transient abort or quarantine and leave previous pointer readable), A-07 quarantine-failure-as-hard-error, and the snake_case serde round-trip.

**Check result:** `cargo check -p application` reports 0 errors in `activation.rs`; the 12 errors are all in `crates/ports/src/platform.rs` (missing types) and are explicitly out of scope per task rules.
